===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An act of [[dodging]].
# A [[trick]], [[evasion]] or [[wile]]. (Now mainly in the expression {{m|en|tax dodge}}.)
#* {{RQ:Thackeray Pendennis||passage=The '''dodges''' of women beat all comprehension; and I am sure she wouldn’t let the lad off so easily, if she had not some other scheme on hand.|12}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1869|journal=Punch|volume=57|page=257
|passage=“Ain't this a rum go? This is a queer sort of '''dodge''' for lighting the streets.”}}
#* {{RQ:Corelli Sorrows of Satan|edition=US|page=14|text=He knows everybody, and is up to all the '''dodges''' of editorial management and newspaper cliques.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A line of work.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1992|journal=Time|volume=140|issue=1-9|page=74
|passage=In the marketing '''dodge''', that is known as rub-off.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Chris Knopf|title=Head Wounds|page=233
|passage=Through a series of unconventional circumstances, some my fault, Jackie had found herself working both civil and criminal sides of the real estate '''dodge''', which put her among a rare breed of attorney {{...}}}}

